      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOCKSLEY CAVALIER (4) finished second last start, beaten 2.25 metres, in a nice return to form at Melton over 1720m when second-up from a break. Should be close to peak fitness and looks ready to strike. EL TORNADO (2) won two runs back then things went sour last time when he broke and finished a long way back in seventh over 2100m at Geelong. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. With manners he is talented enough to be competitive. KENNYS SON (8) is worth plenty of thought off a last-start win by 2.25 metres at Melton, his second success from his last three outings. AGAINST THE BRIDLE (10) continues to race well, finishing fourth from a wide draw last time and winning four of his prevision five. Each way hope with even luck from the back row.",
